/ A module's type is named by its module (ruling 7, decisions 752 + 761). A type's name
/ is its namespace read from a root, like a file path, with no search for a unique tail.
/ A module's main type takes the module's name (decision 761): the window module's
/ primary type is named `window`; a type inside another module's folder is reached by
/ that module (screen's window kind is `screen.window`). A written name is a path —
/ bare `page` reaches no type, because the window module's page is `window.page`.
ModuleTypeIsNamedByItsModule
- set %w% = %!app.type["window"]%
- assert %w.name% equals "window"
- set %sw% = %!app.type["screen.window"]%
- assert %sw.name% equals "screen.window"
- set %none% = %!app.type["page"]%
- assert %none% is null
